  "goodToKnow": "Der Insasse (die Insassin) is an occupant of a vehicle (die Insassen des Wagens) or an inmate of a prison or institution: die Insassen der Justizvollzugsanstalt. It's typical of police and news reports: Die beiden Insassen wurden leicht verletzt. It's a weak noun: den Insassen, des Insassen. Car insurance often includes eine Insassenunfallversicherung. The word comes from an old form meaning one who sits inside."
